Wow! Thank you!

This almost accomplishes what I am after. A few things:

1. I think you have to specify the yearlySiteCovs:

ammaMF <- formatLong(amma, type = "unmarkedMultFrame", numPrimary = 5, yearlySiteCovs = visit)

Otherwise, they do not appear in ammaMF

2. The covariates need to be transformed. I note in your teaching post that you had done the following:

covars <- select(occ2012, -date, -site, -observer, -spp, -count, -year, -visit, -wind)
covar_meds <- apply(covars, 2, median)
covar_mads <- apply(covars, 2, mad)
# Now scale them in the original data set
which_cols <- which(names(occ2012) %in% names(covar_meds)) # Identifies columns to standardize
occ2012[, which_cols] <- median_scale(occ2012[, which_cols])

I took the following approach (changed here from my original script:

# Standardizing covariates Mean-Xi/SD (see Wilson and Schmidt. (2015).Ecosphere 6(9):168. )
# Obtain covariates
covars <- select(FWCPdata, wetdist.3, cutdist.4, rddist.5)

# Now scale them in the original data set
which_cols <- which(names(FWCPdata) %in% names(covars)) # Identifies columns to standardize
covar_mean <- apply(covars, 2, mean, na.rm = TRUE)
covar_sd <- apply(covars, 2, sd, na.rm = TRUE)
covar_wet <- (covar_mean[1] - (apply(covars[1], 2, function(x) x)))/covar_sd[1]
covar_cut <- (covar_mean[2] - (apply(covars[2], 2, function(x) x)))/covar_sd[2]
covar_rd <- (covar_mean[3] - (apply(covars[3], 2, function(x) x)))/covar_sd[3]
FWCPdata[, which_cols] <- cbind(covar_wet,covar_cut,covar_rd)

It seems necessary to scale the covariates. However, ammaMF output looks as follows:

